---
import JournalLayout from '../../layouts/JournalLayout.astro';

const lang = 'en';
---

<JournalLayout
  title="For Authors | Ayamatma"
  description="Author guidelines for Ayamatma: Journal of Vedantic Studies."
  lang={lang}
>
  <section class="section stack">
    <p class="eyebrow">For Authors</p>
    <h1 class="section-title">For Authors</h1>
    <p class="muted">
      Submissions should be clear, sourced, disciplined, and honest about genre.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Article categories</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Research articles:</strong> peer-reviewed scholarly articles with explicit argument and sources.</li>
        <li><strong>Editor-reviewed essays:</strong> analytical essays reviewed by the editor or assigned editorial reader.</li>
        <li><strong>Translations and commentaries:</strong> source-based textual work with Sanskrit/transliteration and interpretive notes.</li>
        <li><strong>Critical reviews:</strong> reviews of books, articles, public claims, or debates.</li>
        <li><strong>Dialogues and reflections:</strong> interviews, conversations, and reflective pieces clearly marked by genre.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Submission expectations</h2>
      <p>Submissions should include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Title, author name, affiliation if any, and contact email.</li>
        <li>Article category.</li>
        <li>Abstract of 100–250 words for research articles and long essays.</li>
        <li>Keywords.</li>
        <li>Clear distinction between quotation, translation, paraphrase, interpretation, and speculation.</li>
        <li>Full citation details for primary and secondary sources.</li>
        <li>Disclosure of prior publication, conflicts of interest, and use of AI tools where relevant.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Style</h2>
      <p>
        Ayamatma favors direct prose, precise definitions, and limited jargon. Sanskrit terms should be
        transliterated consistently using IAST where possible. Authors may use Devanāgarī or other Indian
        scripts when useful, but transliteration and translation should also be provided for accessibility.
      </p>

      <h2>Review outcome</h2>
      <p>
        Possible decisions are accept, accept with minor revision, revise and resubmit, reject with invitation
        to reconceive, or reject. The review path will be recorded by article category.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</JournalLayout>
